    "I_3_stays_nonnegative_on_all_examples": true,
    "certified_path_to_s_gt_3": false,
    "reason": "Lemma 4.3 needs I_s(\u03bd)\u22650 for every \u03bd \u22a5 radial. Two-shell \u2113=1 measures give I_s<0 for every s>3 (interval enclosure of the closed quadratic form; s=4 is the exact rational \u22121025/2048). Hardy is applied to u=|x|^{s/2} V, not to V. Q_H(V) stays near 4.5 and does not control the sign of I_s. For the s=3.1 dipole, Q_H(u) < (3.1)\u00b2/4 already, so there is no uniform gap past 9/4. Lemma 5.9 (\u03b1_N vs \u03b2, 2\u2264s\u22644) does not replace radialization. A 3D search is only an upper bound on \u03b2_s.",
